{"name":"Butter Cookie","hex":"#f0e4b2","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"butter","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A soft, fatty foodstuff made by churning the cream of milk (generally cow's milk).","Any of various foodstuffs made from other foods or oils, similar in consistency to, eaten like or intended as a substitute for butter (preceded by the name of the food used to make it)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To spread butter on.","To move one's weight backwards or forwards onto the tips or tails of one's skis or snowboard so only the tip or tail is in contact with the snow. Similar to applying butter to bread with the end of a knife.\nTo spin on skis or a snowboard using only the tips or tails being in contact with the snow"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/butter"},{"term":"cookie","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A small, flat, baked good which is either crisp or soft but firm.","A sweet baked good (as in the previous sense) usually having chocolate chips, fruit, nuts, etc. baked into it."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To send a cookie to (a user, computer, etc.)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cookie"}],"entries":[{"title":"Butter cookie","blocks":[{"text":"Butter cookies, also known as Danish butter cookies, are a type of cookie or biscuit originating in Denmark consisting of butter, flour, and sugar. They are similar to shortbread biscuit."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e5/2019-11-29_14_52_43_The_interior_of_a_tin_of_McKenzie_%26_Lloyds_Danish_Style_Butter_Cookies_in_the_Dulles_section_of_Sterling%2C_Loudoun_County%2C_Virginia.jpg/330px-2019-11-29_14_52_43_The_interior_of_a_tin_of_McKenzie_%26_Lloyds_Danish_Style_Butter_Cookies_in_the_Dulles_section_of_Sterling%2C_Loudoun_County%2C_Virginia.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Butter_cookie","wikidata":"Q1038537"},{"title":"Butter","blocks":[{"text":"Butter is a dairy product made from the fat and protein components of churned cream. It is a semi-solid emulsion at room temperature, consisting of approximately 81% butterfat. It is used at room temperature as a spread, melted as a condiment, and used as a fat in baking, sauce-making, pan frying, and other cooking procedures."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/%C5%A0v%C3%A9dsk%C3%BD_kol%C3%A1%C4%8D_naruby_904_%28cropped%29.JPG/330px-%C5%A0v%C3%A9dsk%C3%BD_kol%C3%A1%C4%8D_naruby_904_%28cropped%29.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Butter","wikidata":"Q34172"},{"title":"Cookie","blocks":[{"text":"A cookie is a sweet biscuit with high sugar and fat content. Cookie dough is softer than that used for other types of biscuit, and they are cooked longer at lower temperatures. The dough typically contains flour, sugar, egg, and some type of oil or fat. It may include other ingredients such as raisins, oats, chocolate chips, or nuts. Cookie texture varies from crisp and crunchy to soft and chewy, depending on the exact combination of ingredients and methods used to create them."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/2ChocolateChipCookies.jpg/330px-2ChocolateChipCookies.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cookie","wikidata":"Q13266"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/46/Cookie_ingredients_like_flour_and_butter.jpg/500px-Cookie_ingredients_like_flour_and_butter.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/46/Cookie_ingredients_like_flour_and_butter.jpg/1280px-Cookie_ingredients_like_flour_and_butter.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/46/Cookie_ingredients_like_flour_and_butter.jpg/500px-Cookie_ingredients_like_flour_and_butter.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Butter and flour","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACookie_ingredients_like_flour_and_butter.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1b/Buttered_crumpet3.jpg/500px-Buttered_crumpet3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1b/Buttered_crumpet3.jpg/1280px-Buttered_crumpet3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1b/Buttered_crumpet3.jpg/500px-Buttered_crumpet3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Butter spread on a crumpet using a butter knife","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AButtered_crumpet3.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7e/Churning_butter.jpg/500px-Churning_butter.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7e/Churning_butter.jpg/1280px-Churning_butter.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7e/Churning_butter.jpg/500px-Churning_butter.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Churning cream into butter using a hand-held mixer","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AChurning_butter.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/43/Butterschmalz-2.jpg/500px-Butterschmalz-2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/43/Butterschmalz-2.jpg/1280px-Butterschmalz-2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org